 "machine_note": "A Linux VM on the team's laptop: 2 vCPUs of an AMD Ryzen 5 5600H, 3 GB RAM. Not the deployment hardware. Repeated runs on this VM varied by about 10%.",
 "capture_note": "Single-host captures taken on the laptop itself. Two of the three have average packet sizes above the 1,514-byte Ethernet maximum (1,610 and 4,202 bytes): the capture holds segments coalesced by the network card, so their Mbps is higher than wire-size packets would give. Packets/s and flows/s are the figures to compare. Flow counts are low because one host's traffic has few flows; the synthetic benchmark is the flow-heavy case.",
